{"id":"h14t3","name":"Match Refunds to Payments","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The table <b>payments</b> has the columns <code>payment_id</code>, <code>customer_id</code>, <code>paid_at</code> (timestamp), <code>amount</code> and <code>status</code> (<code>'ok'</code> or <code>'failed'</code>; failed payments do not exist for this report). The table <b>refunds</b> has the columns <code>refund_id</code>, <code>customer_id</code>, <code>refunded_at</code> (timestamp) and <code>amount</code>.</p>\n<p>Refunds are matched to payments <b>one to one</b>, by customer and exact amount: for a customer and an amount, the 1st refund (by <code>refunded_at</code>, then <code>refund_id</code>) is matched with the 1st payment (by <code>paid_at</code>, then <code>payment_id</code>), the 2nd refund with the 2nd payment, and so on.</p>\n<p>Each refund gets a <code>status</code>:</p>\n<ul><li><code>'NO_PAYMENT'</code> when there is no payment with its rank;</li>\n<li><code>'REFUND_BEFORE_PAYMENT'</code> when the matched payment is not strictly before the refund (suspicious);</li>\n<li><code>'MATCHED'</code> otherwise.</li></ul>\n<p>Your task is to return one row per refund with the columns <code>refund_id</code>, <code>customer_id</code>, <code>amount</code>, <code>payment_id</code> and <code>minutes_after_payment</code> (whole minutes from the payment to the refund) — both <code>NULL</code> unless the status is <code>'MATCHED'</code> — and <code>status</code>, sorted by <code>refund_id</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>payments</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>payment_id</th><th>customer_id</th><th>paid_at</th><th>amount</th><th>status</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 08:00:00</td><td>50</td><td>ok</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 08:30:00</td><td>50</td><td>ok</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 08:40:00</td><td>20</td><td>failed</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>2</td><td>2026-03-02 16:20:00</td><td>99.9</td><td>ok</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 08:45:00</td><td>20</td><td>ok</td></tr></table></div><p>Table <code>refunds</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>refund_id</th><th>customer_id</th><th>refunded_at</th><th>amount</th></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 09:40:00</td><td>50</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 09:30:00</td><td>50</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 11:20:00</td><td>50</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>2</td><td>2026-03-02 14:40:00</td><td>99.9</td></tr><tr><td>14</td><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 08:41:00</td><td>20</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>refund_id</th><th>customer_id</th><th>amount</th><th>payment_id</th><th>minutes_after_payment</th><th>status</th></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>1</td><td>50.0</td><td>2</td><td>70</td><td>MATCHED</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>1</td><td>50.0</td><td>1</td><td>90</td><td>MATCHED</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>1</td><td>50.0</td><td>null</td><td>null</td><td>NO_PAYMENT</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>2</td><td>99.9</td><td>null</td><td>null</td><td>REFUND_BEFORE_PAYMENT</td></tr><tr><td>14</td><td>1</td><td>20.0</td><td>null</td><td>null</td><td>REFUND_BEFORE_PAYMENT</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> tables <code>payments</code>, <code>refunds</code><br><b>[output]</b> the result of one query with exactly the columns <code>refund_id</code>, <code>customer_id</code>, <code>amount</code>, <code>payment_id</code>, <code>minutes_after_payment</code>, <code>status</code>, in this order; rows in the order given by the statement</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["appariement 1 pour 1","ROW_NUMBER des deux côtés","LEFT JOIN","statuts","minutes entre deux horodatages"],"minutes":20,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>query.sql</code>. Efface le commentaire de départ si tu veux.</li><li>Écris <b>une seule requête</b> qui commence par <code>SELECT</code> (ou <code>WITH</code>). Les tables <code>payments</code>, <code>refunds</code> existent déjà, remplies avec les données du test : pas de <code>CREATE TABLE</code> ni d'<code>INSERT</code>.</li><li>Le moteur est PostgreSQL. Si tu écris plusieurs requêtes, seul le résultat de la dernière est noté.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Le résultat de ta requête doit avoir <b>exactement 6 colonnes</b>, avec ces noms et dans cet ordre : <code>refund_id</code>, <code>customer_id</code>, <code>amount</code>, <code>payment_id</code>, <code>minutes_after_payment</code>, <code>status</code>. Une colonne en plus (une colonne de calcul oubliée), un nom différent ou un autre ordre et le test est faux, même si les valeurs sont justes. Nomme chaque colonne calculée avec <code>AS</code>.</li><li><b>L'ordre des lignes compte</b> : trie exactement comme l'énoncé le demande (<code>ORDER BY</code> à la fin de la requête).</li><li>Valeurs : les nombres sont comparés à 0,000001 près : arrondis seulement là où l'énoncé le demande, et au nombre de décimales demandé ; une case vide attendue s'écrit <code>null</code> : ce n'est ni <code>0</code> ni une chaîne vide.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 8 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"payments":{"columns":[["payment_id","INT"],["customer_id","INT"],["paid_at","TIMESTAMP"],["amount","NUMERIC(10,2)"],["status","TEXT"]],"rows":[[1,1,"2026-03-02 08:00:00",50,"ok"],[2,1,"2026-03-02 08:30:00",50,"ok"],[3,1,"2026-03-02 08:40:00",20,"failed"],[4,2,"2026-03-02 16:20:00",99.9,"ok"],[5,1,"2026-03-02 08:45:00",20,"ok"]]},"refunds":{"columns":[["refund_id","INT"],["customer_id","INT"],["refunded_at","TIMESTAMP"],["amount","NUMERIC(10,2)"]],"rows":[[10,1,"2026-03-02 09:40:00",50],[11,1,"2026-03-02 09:30:00",50],[12,1,"2026-03-02 11:20:00",50],[13,2,"2026-03-02 14:40:00",99.9],[14,1,"2026-03-02 08:41:00",20]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["refund_id","customer_id","amount","payment_id","minutes_after_payment","status"],"rows":[[10,1,50.0,2,70,"MATCHED"],[11,1,50.0,1,90,"MATCHED"],[12,1,50.0,null,null,"NO_PAYMENT"],[13,2,99.9,null,null,"REFUND_BEFORE_PAYMENT"],[14,1,20.0,null,null,"REFUND_BEFORE_PAYMENT"]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"payments":{"columns":[["payment_id","INT"],["customer_id","INT"],["paid_at","TIMESTAMP"],["amount","NUMERIC(10,2)"],["status","TEXT"]],"rows":[[1,3,"2026-03-02 08:00:00",10,"ok"]]},"refunds":{"columns":[["refund_id","INT"],["customer_id","INT"],["refunded_at","TIMESTAMP"],["amount","NUMERIC(10,2)"]],"rows":[[1,3,"2026-03-02 08:00:00",10],[2,4,"2026-03-02 08:05:00",10]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["refund_id","customer_id","amount","payment_id","minutes_after_payment","status"],"rows":[[1,3,10.0,null,null,"REFUND_BEFORE_PAYMENT"],[2,4,10.0,null,null,"NO_PAYMENT"]]}}],"hidden_n":8,"hidden":"","solution":""}